Node ID=11 Morality 2
Text=Do humans consider it immoral when a huntsman kills a deer to feed his family? Or is it immoral for a herdsman to keep a flock of sheep or cattle? Of course not. They are above these other animals in the great chain of being and so they have dominion over them. 
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=11 Morality 3
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=11 Morality 2 Feralkin
Text=You of all people should understand, beast-man. Nature is red in tooth and claw. Do humans consider it immoral when a huntsman kills a deer to feed his family? Of course not. They are above these other animals and so they have dominion over them. 
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=11 Morality 3
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=11 Morality 3
Text=We, as titans, are above mere humans in the chain of being and so they are not fit to judge us by their standards. It is important you realize this. 
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Custom Requirement=CUseCannedExpressionExpression
{
Canned Expression=Dialog/Requirements/Attributes/IN 7+
}
Reply Text=Even if we assume what you say is true, is it still not immoral to needlessly torment another living being irrespective of its location on your "great chain." 
Go to node ID=12 Needless torment smart
Action work in progress=show only if high intelligence

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I don't care what you think, destroying this town was evil. 
Go to node ID=13 Needless torment dumb
Action work in progress=show only if not high int

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What gives you the right to determine who is above or below you? 
Go to node ID=15 Might makes right

Requirement=!None
