Node ID=30 History 2
Text=In the old days, many thousands of years ago, magic was a fundamental part of the world. It wasn't viewed with mistrust as it is today, it was as natural as the sky or grass.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=
Go to node ID=30 History 3
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 History 3
Text=In those days humankind was first learning to bind spirits and wield magic. Tragically, their ability to use its power increased much more quickly than their wisdom. Over the course of centuries magic began to grow out of control, taking on an elemental mind of its own until soon the world was little more than a playground for powerful spirits.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Custom Requirement=CHasSpirit
{
Spirit=Spirits/Ancestral
}
Reply Text=The spirit I carry is one of my own dead. Is that the binding you mean?
Go to node ID=30 spirit ancestral
Icon=Attribute Icon

Requirement=!None
Custom Requirement=CHasSpirit
{
Spirit=Spirits/Beastial
}
Reply Text=Mine is no ancestor. It is a beast, and it was in the world before either of us.
Go to node ID=30 spirit beastial
Icon=Attribute Icon

Requirement=!None
Custom Requirement=CHasSpirit
{
Spirit=Spirits/Demonic
}
Reply Text=The thing bound to me is neither an ancestor nor a beast.
Go to node ID=30 spirit demonic
Icon=Attribute Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What happened?
Go to node ID=30 Utnapishtim
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 spirit ancestral
Text=Yes, and of the three thefts your people learned, it is the gentlest: you keep your grandmother in a jar and call it inheritance. Consider what you are carrying, small one. She stood under the sky I have been describing to you. Ask her what it looked like, if anything of her is left that remembers.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Go on with your history.
Go to node ID=30 Utnapishtim
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 spirit beastial
Text=The beast, yes. Older than your line and far simpler in its wants. Rhea's own children wore such shapes when the world was young and we thought no shame in it. But you have bound a piece of the first world to a creature that lives eighty years. Be careful which of you turns out to be the rider.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Go on with your history.
Go to node ID=30 Utnapishtim
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 spirit demonic
Text=<For the first time the titan looks at you with something other than patience.> A demon. Then your kind learned nothing whatever. That is the binding that pulled the sky down on Atlantis, and you wear it into a human village like a travelling coat. Utnapishtim drowned the world for less than what is standing in front of me.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Go on with your history.
Go to node ID=30 Utnapishtim
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 Utnapishtim
Text=Utnapishtim, a powerful sorcerer, took it upon himself to save the world by ridding it of all magic. It was a foolish, evil decision, taken without the counsel of calmer minds. To rid the world of magic, he called down a global cataclysm, a massive worldwide flood that scoured and ravaged all creation.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Custom Requirement=CUseCannedExpressionExpression
{
Canned Expression=Dialog/Requirements/Faction/Inquisitor IS
}
Reply Text=Utnapishtim was the first Inquisitor, then. And the only one who finished the work.
Go to node ID=31 the first inquisitor
Icon=Attribute Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What happened to civilization?
Go to node ID=30 Civilization destroyed by the flood

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What happened to your people?
Go to node ID=30 Civilization destroyed by the flood

Requirement=!None
Custom Requirement=CUseCannedExpressionExpression
{
Canned Expression=Dialog/Requirements/Attributes/IN 6+
}
Reply Text=I have heard a similar story.
