Node ID=31 the first inquisitor
Text=<She is quiet for a moment.> You are the first of your order to say it out loud, and I do not think it flatters either of you. He drowned every city on the earth to be rid of a thing he had not troubled to understand, and your Church has gone on drowning it in smaller batches ever since. He at least had the excuse of an emergency.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=He had the right of it. What happened to your people?
Go to node ID=30 Civilization destroyed by the flood

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I have heard enough of your history.
Go to node ID=39 History end
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 Flood myths
Text=Yes, I have learned many of your human flood myths, though all misinterpret it in one way or another. The Babylonians knew of the Flood, and even the name of its instigator. The Greeks remembered it as the story of Deucalion, and the Hebrews as the story of Noah. Nearly every culture remembers the event, but none still know its purpose. 
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Wasn't everything destroyed?
Go to node ID=30 Civilization destroyed by the flood

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What happened to your people?
Go to node ID=30 Civilization destroyed by the flood

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=That's enough history for one day.
Go to node ID=39 History end

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=A great need to sleep is overwhelming me. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=90 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 Civilization destroyed by the flood
Text=Every civilization -- ours, the Atlanteans, a dozen others -- was destroyed, and magic was banished. In its absence, the race of titans vanished as well, falling into a deep sleep within the womb of our mother, the earth. No titan again walked the world until the Disjunction awoke us. When we reawoke it was as if from a long slumber, and we found ourselves greatly diminished. Some of our kind have become little more than feral beasts.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I think I have met some of these feral titans. Why are you different?
Go to node ID=30 Explanation

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What has happened since then?
Go to node ID=30 Recent history

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I've heard enough. Can we speak of something else?
Go to node ID=39 History end

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I must be going. Goodbye
Go to node ID=90 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=30 Explanation
Text=When we awoke, our race no longer had the might and understanding that we had in the old days. Much of our memory was gone. As elemental creatures of the earth we... possess an impulse to revert to a primal, animalistic state. It is only by strong custom and constant force of will that we remain the civilized paragons you see before you here. This is why it is vital that you assist Lethos.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What does this have to do with Lethos?
Go to node ID=30 memory transition

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=What has happened since the reawakening?
Go to node ID=30 Recent history

