Node ID=50 Memory
Text=Memory is the core of our society. A titan's memories are written in his mneme, a crystal deep within his chest. When he dies, this crystal is consumed by a special member of the tribe, the Memnosesthion, or "eater of memories."  
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=You're cannibals?
Go to node ID=55 Titans aren't cannibals

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Tell me about the Memnosesthion.
Go to node ID=51 Memnosesthion
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=51 Memnosesthion
Text=He is responsible for keeping within his mneme the collective memory of all the past members of the tribe. He is the guardian of tradition, the living center of our civilization. Without his knowledge we would, over the course of but a few generations, revert to a... less civilized state, like the lost tribes of the Pyrenees. As our cultural heart, he is held in high esteem and lives a life of luxury, zealously protected from all harm by the rest of the tribe.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=It sounds like a good job.
Go to node ID=52 Price of memory

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=How could one individual handle so many memories?
Go to node ID=56 Many memories

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I must be going. Goodbye.
Go to node ID=90 Goodbye
Icon=Exit Icon
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=52 Price of memory
Text=There is a cost. In return for the many privelages accorded to him, the Memnosesthion has a sacred obligation. Late in life we titans, much like your species, are prone to forgetfulness. The mind, memory, starts to fade. This, you might imagine, poses a particular problem for the individual charged with harboring the memories and culture of the entire tribe. 
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=If his memory were lost, it would be like losing the history of your tribe.
Go to node ID=53 Sacrifice
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=53 Sacrifice
Text=It is the Memnosesthion's duty to submit to a ritual sacrifice before age begins to rob him of the tribe's memory, so that his still-pristine mneme can be passed on intact to the next generation. It is a heavy burden to bear, but one that is chosen, not thrust upon the titan who takes it up.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Custom Requirement=CHasPerkExpression
{
Perks To Check For=Array
{
Item Count=1
Perk To Check For=Perks/!Event Title Perks/Necromancer
}
}
Reply Text=You cut a crystal out of a living elder and swallow it so the dead keep speaking. My art has a name for that, and your Church has a fire for it.
Go to node ID=53 necromancer
Icon=Speach Skill Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Why not simply learn to read? You could write your history and not rely on memories.
Go to node ID=56 Titans are literate

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Does this have something to do with why you are here?
